<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charlemagne</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 747–814</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charlemagne was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a> from 768 and was crowned emperor in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-leo-iii">Pope Leo III</a> in 800. He conquered much of western and central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, and promoted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-renaissance">Carolingian Renaissance</a>. He exchanged embassies with the Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harun-al-rashid">Harun al-Rashid</a>, and his imperial title was later claimed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charlemagne.jpg" alt="Charlemagne" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charlemagne. Autorité émettrice de monnaie indéterminé. Atelier monétaire. Émetteur · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Charlemagne_denier_Mayence_812_814.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
